<title>BAHRAIN: Saudi 52-week T-bill falls to 5.9642 pct.</title>
<headline>Saudi 52-week T-bill falls to 5.9642 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yield on 52-week Saudi treasury bills worth 500 million riyals fell to 5.9642 percent from 6.1731 percent last month, a banker said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bills are offered once a month by the Saudi Arabian Monetary Agency to Saudi-based banks.</p>
<p>The average price rose to 94.3125 from 94.1250.</p>
<p>One-year Saudi riyal interbank deposit rates were quoted at 6-1/16, 5-15/16 percent.</p>
</text>
